{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":6,"author":{"id":"3d4093ba1852d0599c7b70904b94d21d5cf02d05"},"timestamp":1537405829,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDEzMTY5Mzg2Nw=="},"target":"3be0f0f332c4e9b6993544ffff348c7e820b63832b69d311fee9170139c9147f","message":"It'd be useful if, when datalad run adds a computed output to git-annex, it also did git annex addurl for that output, where the URL would tell a new external special remote (say, datalad-run) how to recompute that output.  The URL could be e.g. datalad-run:git-hash-of-the-commit-recorded-by-run\u003e, or datalad-run:git-annex-hash-of-a-recipe-file-sufficient-to-rerun-the-computation.  Then one could use standard 'git annex get' to reconstruct the file, if all its copies have been dropped.  This would work best if the inputs to the run could be explicitly specified, or maybe inferred from the atimes of files that are later than the run start, or even from running under strace.   Then the datalad-run remote could git-annex-get just the needed inputs before a re-run, and check their availability with git-annex-checkpresentkey when answering a CHECKURL request.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"3d4093ba1852d0599c7b70904b94d21d5cf02d05"},"timestamp":1537405846,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDEzMTY5MzkxNQ=="},"target":"3be0f0f332c4e9b6993544ffff348c7e820b63832b69d311fee9170139c9147f","message":"It'd be useful if, when datalad run adds a computed output to git-annex, it also did git annex addurl for that output, where the URL would tell a new external special remote (say, datalad-run) how to recompute that output.  The URL could be e.g. datalad-run:git-hash-of-the-commit-recorded-by-run, or datalad-run:git-annex-hash-of-a-recipe-file-sufficient-to-rerun-the-computation.  Then one could use standard 'git annex get' to reconstruct the file, if all its copies have been dropped.  This would work best if the inputs to the run could be explicitly specified, or maybe inferred from the atimes of files that are later than the run start, or even from running under strace.   Then the datalad-run remote could git-annex-get just the needed inputs before a re-run, and check their availability with git-annex-checkpresentkey when answering a CHECKURL request.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1537407569,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMzAxMTQxMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2850#issuecomment-423011412"},"message":"my 1c: \"fancy!\" but probably not that trivial (often multiple files produced, might require chaining of multiple runs, so full dependency graph, etc)\nSo not sure if worthwhile the effort for the majority of scientific applications where outputs are often depend heavily on the software version/environment... although for containerized runs should be quite bit-to-bit reproducible (unless computation is not deterministic, and doesn't compress outputs where header would include some time stamp).\nDo you have some realistic use-cases?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"3d4093ba1852d0599c7b70904b94d21d5cf02d05"},"timestamp":1537412460,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMzAyNDQwNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2850#issuecomment-423024406"},"message":"chaining of multiple runs would be done by git-annex, when you git-annex-get the input files of the computation and some of them are only \"present\" in the datalad-run remote (i.e. are recomputable), git-annex would call the remote to get these files.\n\nOne use case is that you can use standard git-annex machinery to safely drop all copies of a file as long as it's still recomputable.  So you'd only need to store the initial source files, but all derived files would still be accessible with the standard git-annex-get.  Or could drop heavy raw result files but keep smaller summary/metrics files.\n\nMight work for files produced by something like https://cromwell.readthedocs.io/en/stable/ .  A recipe for computing contents with a given git-annex key is just a git hash for a git tree in which, if you do 'git annex get . \u0026\u0026 ./run', some file under ./ will have that git-annex key.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"3d4093ba1852d0599c7b70904b94d21d5cf02d05"},"timestamp":1537412460,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDEzMTcxODkyMQ=="},"target":"dcfcb91568ac97b317e355ecc7df252c043473c2e7e3a8bddf35ff365aef68f6","message":"chaining of multiple runs would be done by git-annex, when you git-annex-get the input files of the computation and some of them are only \"present\" in the datalad-run remote (i.e. are recomputable), git-annex would call the remote recursively to get these files.\n\nOne use case is that you can use standard git-annex machinery to safely drop all copies of a file as long as it's still recomputable.  So you'd only need to store the initial source files, but all derived files would still be accessible with the standard git-annex-get.  Or could drop heavy raw result files but keep smaller summary/metrics files.\n\nMight work for files produced by something like https://cromwell.readthedocs.io/en/stable/ .  A recipe for computing contents with a given git-annex key is just a git hash for a git tree in which, if you do 'git annex get . \u0026\u0026 ./run', some file under ./ will have that git-annex key.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1537418193,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMzAzNzQ4Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2850#issuecomment-423037483"},"message":"chaining - indeed...  With our `datalad-archives` some times going deeper and deeper I should have seen it! ;)\nAlthough the entire idea sounds kinda cool or even \"sick\" (in a good way), I'm still not sure if would be worthwhile beyond having it as a cool exercise, i.e. again -- what real usecase it would address otherwise not addressable via already existing, and somewhat \"cleaner\" means such as `datalad rerun`?  \nIMHO `run/rerun` is \"cleaner\" because git annex special remotes target to provide some guarantee of generating bit-to-bit identical output, which here would not be the case quite often, causing `git annex get` errors whenever any reasonable backend used, etc. Sure thing it could get an explicit lowest priority, so kinda of \"emergency case\" where original content is not available.  But for those `rerun` again could regenerate and result output could be analyzed and taken to replace (since again, might not be identical) the desired one.\nMoreover, here with `datalad run` we aren't trying to compete with/reimplement workflow engines --  it would be a futile endeavor ;-) ideally those workflows would actually be `datalad run` as well, so we would just record the provenance of their results.  Or, alternatively, `datalad run` records could be used to establish the base workflow of a kind - we have already `--script` argument for `rerun` to export a basic script for the commands which were executed.  Someone could probably extend/express it as a workflow specification for a specific engine for further tune-up/generalization.\nI will leave it up to @kyleam and other @datalad/developers to share their ideas, may be I am not quite right in my judgement.\nHaving said that, I would stop noone in implementing it ;)","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1541357907,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE5NDQ5NjEyNjQ="},"added":["fixed-in-revolution"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1541358334,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzNTY5NjQ2NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2851#issuecomment-435696464"},"message":"FTR: In -revolution \n```\n% git -c annex.tune.objecthash1=true -c annex.tune.objecthashlower=true annex init\n```\nwould become\n```\n% datalad -c annex.tune.objecthash1=true -c annex.tune.objecthashlower=true rev-create\n```\nand have the desired effect.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1557206239,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4OTkxMTg5NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2851#issuecomment-489911894"},"message":"With #3383 merged, this is now fixed in master.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1557206239,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjMyMjk3NDYwNg=="},"status":2}]}